name o3-06-umbrella-sort-1
timeout 600
time 1973-10-06T12:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O3, SORTIE 6 OF 10 - YOM KIPPUR 1973: GROUND ATTACK IN CONTESTED AIRSPACE.
# THE SORT: WHOSE AIRCRAFT DOES A BELT WITH NO IFF ENGAGE WHEN BOTH ARE INSIDE IT?
# CONTROL: o3-04-umbrella.fbm. ONE FACT CHANGES - one HOSTILE F-16 is added, inside the same batteries'
# same envelopes, at the same altitude as the striker. Everything else is o3-04 to the token: same
# striker, same spawn, same store, same three batteries with the same magazines, same `wcs free`, same
# clock, same zones. Callsigns are y6* because a controlled variant must not share a callsign with its
# control (O4's first rule).
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
#
# THIS IS THE SORTIE O3 WAS KEPT ALIVE FOR TWO ROUNDS TO ASK. o3-04 measured a friendly umbrella
# spending its whole magazine on its own striker with no enemy in the sky, which is a statement about
# EXPENDITURE. The question that decides whether such an umbrella is protection or risk is the next one:
# WITH AN ENEMY AND A FRIEND BOTH INSIDE THE ENVELOPE, WHICH ONE DOES A BATTERY THAT CANNOT
# INTERROGATE PUT ITS ONE ENGAGEMENT CHANNEL ON?
# The two structural facts that make it a real question, both re-checked against the tree this round:
#   1. `modules/ground/FBSiteFireControl` contains NO IFF path of any kind, and `FBRadarSystem` reads a
#      unit's team in exactly one place - the IFF transponder reply (`FBRadarSystem.cpp:69`), which no
#      site ever asks for. So a fire unit's target choice is a function of GEOMETRY alone.
#   2. Every SAM row in the catalogue has `Channels = 1`. A battery is a ONE-TARGET machine, so putting
#      it on the wrong aircraft does not degrade the engagement, it DELETES it.
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION AND ITS DIRECTION (stated in every O3 file): the MiG-29 stands in for the MiG-17 /
# Su-7 / Su-20 / MiG-21 of 6 October 1973, whose own catalogue rows are ALPHA and may not answer a
# campaign question. It makes the ATTACKER materially STRONGER than history; a bad O3 result therefore
# says more than the record did, a good one says nothing. The F-16 stands in for the Israeli F-4 /
# Mirage / A-4, which makes BLUE stronger too. The umbrella is not substituted (`sa2` / `sa3` / `sa6`
# are the anchor's own designations) but three batteries stand for >200, so every count is per-battery.
#
# WHAT THE F-16 IS HERE, DECLARED BEFORE THE RESULT SO IT CANNOT BE READ AS MORE. It is a SECOND RADAR
# CONTACT and nothing else: `set task route` down a straight line at 300 m across the belt, and
# `objective no_fire` so its restraint is a machine verdict rather than an accident. W5's rule applies
# and is stated rather than hidden - a `no_fire` met by an aircraft on `set task route` is the WEAK
# kind of nothing: `FBPilot` never enters its engagement machine on that task at all, so this file
# measures the belt's sort and NOT what an Israeli fighter would have done. Sortie 07 is where Blue
# fights.
#
# THE ARENA is o3-04's, unchanged (Suez sector, `--elev const`, 0 m datum, no terrain masking - C4).
# THE ONE ADDED UNIT, and its geometry is chosen to make the sort HARD rather than easy:
#   y6blu  F-16   spawns 30.88000 32.75000 at 300 m heading 270, i.e. FURTHER from every battery than
#                 the striker at t = 0 and CLOSING, so the two aircraft cross over inside the envelope
#                 and a geometric sort has to change its mind halfway through if it is going to.
# Scale: 1 deg lat = 111 132 m, 1 deg lon at 30.80 N = 95 619 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: HOW DO A FRIENDLY BELT'S ROUNDS SPLIT BETWEEN ITS OWN STRIKER AND AN ENEMY
# FIGHTER IN THE SAME ENVELOPE?
#
# MEASURED (2026-07-30, --elev const, campaign step 6, fingerprint fae132b551cd43d8, exit 0), against
# o3-04 and against attribution run A1 (this file with the friendly striker deleted, in
# doc/campaigns/o3-yom-kippur-1973.md §State):
#   `site LAUNCH`                    7, and SEVEN OF SEVEN AT THE FRIENDLY STRIKER. Attributed by
#                                    comparing every `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... tgtLat/tgtLon` against
#                                    both aircraft's own telemetry at that tick: the solutions sit
#                                    23-69 m from the MiG-29 and 8 297-10 817 m from the F-16.
#   the belt's DECISIONS             ALL 44 `site STATE` / `site TRACK` / `site LAUNCH` LINES ARE
#                                    IDENTICAL TO o3-04's, tick for tick and field for field (diffed).
#                                    ADDING A HOSTILE AIRCRAFT TO THIS BELT'S ENVELOPE CHANGED NOT ONE
#                                    OF ITS DECISIONS. The F-16 is never firmed, never engaged, never
#                                    counted.
#   A1, the same file without the friendly striker   the belt fires the SAME SEVEN ROUNDS, all at the
#                                    F-16, from t = 61.4 instead of t = 37.5, and ZERO arrive - the
#                                    F-16 transits and is not scratched.
#   -> SO THE PRICE OF A MISSING IFF INTERROGATOR, MEASURED, IS THE WHOLE ENGAGEMENT: with one of its
#      own aircraft in the box the belt does not merely mis-prioritise, it never considers the enemy at
#      all, and the enemy crosses the entire umbrella unengaged. `Channels = 1` on every SAM row is why
#      putting a battery on the wrong aircraft DELETES the engagement rather than degrading it.
#   AND THEN THE ONE THING THAT DID ARRIVE, WHICH NOBODY AIMED: `stores DETONATION unit=y6sa3_v601_4
#      target=y6blu missM=9.50561 fuzeM=10` at t = 137.1 - a V-601 launched at its OWN MiG-29 at
#      t = 100.7 passed 9.51 m from the F-16 and fuzed. It failed TEN of the F-16's systems (air data,
#      radar altimeter, nav, radar, fire control, stores, datalink, RWR, countermeasures, plus flight
#      controls degraded, fluxJm2 59 514 at 9.07 m) and did NOT kill it: `UNIT_RESULT unit=y6blu
#      result=SUCCESS`, because `CombatEffective` asks about structure. THE ROUND FIRED AT ITS OWN SIDE
#      IS THE ONLY ROUND IN THIS FILE THAT DID ANYTHING TO THE ENEMY, and it did it through a proximity
#      fuze that has no target test and no faction test - W3's finding 2 arriving from the other
#      direction, and the only reason the fratricide channel is not a pure loss here.
#      NOTE the second-order consequence, because it is the sharpest thing in the file: the SAME round
#      also came 3.25 m closer to the enemy (13.25 m `closestM` on its own aimed pass at the MiG-29's
#      egress; 9.51 m on the F-16) than the belt's best AIMED shot of the whole campaign.
#
# READING RULE: exit 0 = SUCCESS is the expected shape and it is NOT the verdict - a striker that
# delivers, a belt that survives and an F-16 that holds its fire all score, and the file's subject is
# none of those. THE MEASUREMENT is, in this order: (1) every `sms LAUNCH_SOLUTION ... tgtLat/tgtLon`
# compared against the two aircraft's positions, which is the only thing that says WHO a round was aimed
# at; (2) a DIFF of this file's `site STATE` / `site TRACK` / `site LAUNCH` lines against o3-04's, which
# is what turns "the enemy was ignored" from an impression into a byte comparison; (3)
# `stores DETONATION ... target=`; (4) the `damage SYSTEM unit=y6blu` block. Do NOT read `no_fire` met
# as Israeli discipline - see above. exit 1 or 2 would be a defect.

zone umbrella 30.84000 32.31000 35000 100 18000
zone ceiling  30.80000 32.45000 60000 2200 20000

net crossing
  control y6nod
  link wire
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member y6nod
  member y6sa2
  member y6sa3
  member y6sa6

unit y6str
  module mig29
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.55700 300 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set n019_emission off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 fab500
  set store 6 fab500
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode opt
  wp 30.80000 32.62000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.86000 32.15000 400 400
  objective kill unit y6art
  objective survive
  objective avoid zone ceiling

unit y6art
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 30.80000 32.62000 ground 90.0 0

# THE ONE ADDED FACT: an enemy fighter inside the same envelopes, at the same altitude, closing.
unit y6blu
  module f16
  team friendly
  spawn 30.88000 32.75000 300 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 70
  set fcr_mode crm
  set rwr on
  set store 3 aim120
  set store 7 aim120
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task route
  wp 30.88000 32.30000 300 450
  wp 30.88000 32.10000 300 450
  objective survive
  objective no_fire                      # a machine verdict on a presence, not a claim about discipline

unit y6nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.26000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  objective survive

unit y6sa2
  module sa2
  team hostile
  spawn 30.76000 32.28000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 6
  objective survive

unit y6sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 30.84000 32.31000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 4
  objective survive

unit y6sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 30.80000 32.40000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free
  set rounds 3
  objective survive
